ambientAbstractSimplicialComplex -- the ambient simplex
*******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        ambientAbstractSimplicialComplex(K)
  * Inputs:
      * K, an *note abstract simplicial complex: AbstractSimplicialComplex,, 
  * Outputs:
      * an *note abstract simplicial complex: AbstractSimplicialComplex,, 

Description
===========

If an abstract simplicial complex has vertices supported on a subset of $[n] =
\{1,\dots,n\}$, and including $n$, then it seems useful to regard this
simplicial complex as being a subsimplicial complex of the simplex on $[n]$.
This method returns this simplex as the ambient simplicial complex.

+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : K = abstractSimplicialComplex({{1,2},{3}})              |
|                                                             |
|o1 = AbstractSimplicialComplex{-1 => {{}}          }         |
|                               0 => {{1}, {2}, {3}}          |
|                               1 => {{1, 2}}                 |
|                                                             |
|o1 : AbstractSimplicialComplex                               |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : J = ambientAbstractSimplicialComplex(K)                 |
|                                                             |
|o2 = AbstractSimplicialComplex{-1 => {{}}                   }|
|                               0 => {{1}, {2}, {3}}          |
|                               1 => {{1, 2}, {1, 3}, {2, 3}} |
|                               2 => {{1, 2, 3}}              |
|                                                             |
|o2 : AbstractSimplicialComplex                               |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+

